---
description: Apply these rules when adding or modifying GenServers in the supervision tree, especially those that interact with other processes during initialization.
globs: 
alwaysApply: false
---
1. Async Initialization Pattern
NEVER perform synchronous calls to other services in a GenServer's init/1 callback
Use a "two-phase initialization" pattern: basic setup in init/1, then service connections in handle_info/2
Send a :post_init message to self() at the end of init/1 for secondary initialization
2. Supervision Tree Organization
Organize supervisors by dependency requirements, not by functionality
Use multiple supervisors with proper one_for_one strategy rather than a single supervisor
Create explicit supervision hierarchies when services depend on each other
3. GenServer Startup Resilience
Always include error handling in subscription and initialization code
Use try/rescue blocks with explicit logging in critical initialization paths
Implement proper backoff and retry mechanisms for dependent services
4. Process Registration Protocol
Document process registration names and where they're used
Add explicit runtime verification that required processes exist
Provide fallbacks in test environments where processes might not be available